WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.020
A wild rose bush in full bloom.

2
00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.870
Beside it, a dark holly bush.

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:12.060
The poem sets them side by side: "Love
is like the wild rose-briar;" "Friendship

4
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.820
like the holly-tree."

5
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.680
The roses are sweet.

6
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.050
Beside them, the holly
looks dark and plain.

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.270
So if you had to choose, why
would anyone pick the holly?

8
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:28.880
In this mission, you'll see how Emily Brontë
builds a whole poem from one comparison.

9
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.220
You'll find out what spring
and winter mean in this poem.

10
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.480
And you'll hear the
questions the poem asks,

11
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.610
before it gives its answer.

12
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.610
Your mission: explain why
the speaker picks the holly.
